  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reintegration through Integrated Support and Empowerment (RISE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;UNDP is implementing the above project RISE since the 1st of June 2023. This is a joint programme implemented by UNDP (in partnership with the Center for Humanitarian Dialogue (HD) and UNICEF). &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;RISE&#xbf;s overall objective is to address the reintegration needs of vulnerable children, young persons, adults, and other stigmatized groups such as families with perceived ISIL-affiliation returning to Iraq from North-East Syria (NES), as well as of conflict-affected host community members. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The following are the three outputs in RISE joint programme, which also reflect the division of responsibilities among the three implementing partners:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output (1) led by HD: Facilitation of the return of displaced person to Iraq, including ISIL-perceived families, is fostered through dialogues and social cohesion interventions;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output (2) led by UNDP: Families perceived to be affiliated with ISIL/ returning from NES, as well as community members in areas of return received reintegration support;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output (3) led by UNICEF: The protection of child rights, including legal rights, among repatriated Iraqis improved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The total EU contribution for the current action is USD 5,721,000, the remaining commitments amount to US 622,213.80 (the outstanding majority of which are transfers grants to counterparts).&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
